  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.6.3 makes keyed views lighter: a maintained view's result holds one slot per key, and none beyond its identity map when the key is the whole row.\n\n      - **Keyed views:** the result's key index maps each key to one slot rather than a list, and a whole-row key uses the identity map as its index. A view of keys alone holds about 40% less: about 175 B a row where it held 330, in one host's measurements. Counts grow by half again rather than doubling. A key given two rows still faults the view, coded `DeclarationNotHeld`.\n      - **Refresh rows:** `RefreshBuilder` now says what becomes of the rows it is given. A POCO `Replace` holds the collection and reports it through `PocoSource.SnapshotReleased`; `Upsert` and `Delete` read their lists while the refresh runs and hold nothing after `RefreshAsync` returns. The behaviour is unchanged.\n      - **Compatibility:** no change to the API, the protocol or the IR. A 0.6.2 planner serves a 0.6.3 client, and a 0.6.3 planner serves a 0.6.2 client.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.6.3",
